            <ArticleTitle>Association of hemoglobin A(1c) level with the severity of coronary artery disease in patients with diabetes mellitus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>968-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary angiography was performed in 152 men and 163 women with diabetes mellitus (mean age 55 +/- 8 years) because of chest pain. The mean hemoglobin A(1c) level was 6.66 +/- 0.58% in 132 patients with 0-vessel coronary artery disease (CAD), 8.00 +/- 0.84% in 40 patients with 1-vessel CAD, 8.83 +/- 1.45% in 76 patients with 2-vessel CAD, and 10.40 +/- 2.28% in 67 patients with 3- or 4-vessel CAD. There was a significant increasing trend of hemoglobin A(1c) levels over the increasing number of vessels with CAD (p &lt;0.0001).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
